// SOUNDNESS QUEUE — AN `FnOnce` CLOSURE IN A STRUCT FIELD IS CALLED TWICE AND
// THE SECOND CALL FREES WHAT THE FIRST ALREADY MOVED OUT. Tier 1: not an
// admitted aliasing violation but a live double free — the linked binary
// prints `free(): double free detected in tcache 2` and aborts, exit 134.
//
// MEASURED 2026-09-20 on logosc 0.44.0-preview+main-g6dbe3a16: compiles clean
// (rc 0, object written), links, runs, ABORTS. rustc 1.98.1 --edition 2024
// REFUSES the twin with error[E0382]: use of moved value: `h.f`.
//
// THE CARRIER IS THE STRUCT FIELD, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT. The same
// program with the closure in a LOCAL is already refused — sema marks the
// callee moved (`consumes_callee` in lower_call, which asks
// `callable_is_fn_once` and reaches a literal through the binding's
// `VarInfo::closure_id`). A field has no binding, so that route does not
// exist, and the field's TYPE carries no Fn-family kind: a closure type is
// interned by SIGNATURE, and `|| -> String` is the same type whether the
// literal stored in it is `Fn`, `FnMut` or `FnOnce`.
//
// WHAT IT NEEDS: the Fn-family kind on the closure TYPE (a per-literal
// identity inside the Closure TypeRef), which is the repair the
// `KEY-IDENTITY: OPEN #90` note at the kind's own minting site already names
// — `closure_kind_` is keyed by `type_str(ctype)` and takes the MAX across
// every literal of one signature. Then every carrier — local, field, `Box`,
// `dyn` — asks the same question of the same place.
//
// FOUND beside the ADR 0028 call-mode landing (the sema sites that write
// `CallMode` for a closure call). That landing does NOT close this row and
// could not: it fills the mode from the same two routes, and neither reaches
// a field. Rowed under reason 1 of the neighbour rule — the fact has no
// carrier at this site.
package closure_field_fnonce_called_twice_double_free;
use logos.mem.string;

struct H { f: || -> String }

fn main() -> i32 {
    let s: String = String::from("abcd");
    let h = H { f: move || -> String { return s; } };
    let a: String = h.f();
    let b: String = h.f();
    if a.len() != 4i64 { return 1i32; }
    if b.len() != 4i64 { return 2i32; }
    return 0i32;
}
// rustc 1.98.1 --edition 2024: REFUSED — error[E0382]: use of moved value: `h.f`.
